WHAT THIS IS

Object-model stroke 3a's witness (SEQ 219). It prints every Grokking rule and its children in list
order. pop.sh reads the output in shell (a shell compare cannot mis-spell a capture, bear-trap 55) and
asserts two numbers: how many rules carry a builtinActoR (non-zero, the anti-vacuity sibling), and how
many rules have a REAL term after their builtinActoR (the stroke's claim: zero).

Born red on trunk e680c77: the bootstrap called setActions() before adding terms, so builtinActoR sat
at index 1 in twelve rules (recon 11.4). Stroke 3a moves the actor after the terms.

An artifact, for this count, is a child whose tag is one of the minted names (builtinActoR,
builtinParseR, pendingParseR, CodE, BlocK, frameSTAK, tempField, this). Everything else is a term.
